# The build context of EVERY image in this monorepo (Railway root directory `/`).
#
# WHY THE ROOT. Both deployables import mandate/ (the shared grounding store and
# the one embedding module), and a Docker build can only COPY what is inside its
# context. Until 2026-11 each service's context was its brain's directory, and
# each brain kept its own .dockerignore; those rules are merged here, prefixed by
# brain, and the per-brain files are gone (one context, one ignore file).
#
# Each Dockerfile COPYs only its own brain and mandate/, so what this file must
# do is keep the UPLOAD small and keep secrets and data out of every layer.

# ── never in any image ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.git/
.claude/
**/.env
**/.env.*
!policy/.env.example
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/

# ── the site ships to Vercel, not Railway, but capital's ETL READS web/ ───
# (evidenceTiers.json, vocabularies, the guard registry's TS paths: see
# capital/ETL/lib/web_path.py), so its source is in the context. Never its
# dependencies or build output (node_modules/.next above).
web/out/
web/public/data/

# ── capital ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# data/ is carried minus what a run GENERATES: what git tracks there
# (data/guard_registry.json above all) is input the cron reads.
capital/data/*.sqlite
capital/data/*.sqlite-*
capital/data/raw/
capital/data/processed/
capital/data/backups/
capital/data/ranker_cache/
# a database backup must no more enter an image than a credential does
capital/postgres-backup/
# the committed text copy of the authored corpus; restore is a checkout, not a run
capital/corpus-ledger/

# ── policy ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# policy/data/ is the SQLAlchemy package, not a data directory: it stays.
policy/**/*.log
policy/tests/
policy/project-management/
policy/docker-compose.yml
